# MinerTim CLI configuration
# Copy to mining.conf and fill in your values:
#   cp mining.conf.example mining.conf

POOL=pool.supportxmr.com:443
WALLET=YOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS_HERE
# THREADS: leave unset to auto-detect performance cores.
THREADS=
# DONATE_LEVEL: percent of mining time donated (default 5, minimum 1), split
# 50/50 between the MinerTim author and XMRig. See README.
DONATE_LEVEL=5
# NATIVE_LOOP: "on" (default) or "off". Fallback switch for the native-loop JIT,
# which emits the whole 2048-iteration RandomX loop as ARM64 and is worth roughly
# 7% hashrate (aarch64, rx/0, full mode only — ignored elsewhere).
#
# Turn it OFF if the pool starts rejecting shares. A JIT defect does not crash
# the miner: it produces a wrong-but-plausible hash, so the hashrate still looks
# healthy and the only symptom is rejects climbing on the pool dashboard. This
# switch lets you rule the JIT in or out by restarting instead of rebuilding.
# Equivalent to `--native-loop off`, or MINERTIM_NATIVE_LOOP=0 in the environment.
NATIVE_LOOP=
# VERIFY_SHARES: "on" (default) or "off". Before submitting a share, recompute it
# with the older, slower, well-tested code and compare. If they disagree the share
# is withheld and a loud error is logged, so a JIT fault is caught here instead of
# showing up days later as rejected shares on the pool.
#
# Costs about 0.005% of mining time: only the rare hashes good enough to submit
# are re-checked, not the hundreds per second that are discarded. Leave it on.
VERIFY_SHARES=
